\caption(Absent prefix bytes underscore and z select a full four-byte shift. A departure shift skips candidate starts; it does not imply that every byte between those starts was unread.)
\alttext(The shifts for a, b, r, underscore and z are three, two, one, four and four.)

> Boundary controls and a quadratic mismatch family

Matching is case-sensitive on bytes. Embedded NUL and high-byte values are
supported; offsets in UTF-8 are byte offsets, with no decoding or normalization.
Empty and oversized patterns produce no search windows. The trace still
builds their table so it can be inspected.

For text A repeated n times, pattern A repeated m times produces n-m+1
full overlapping matches, each taking m comparisons. Pattern B followed by
m-1 copies of A produces no matches, yet each window compares the m-1 trailing
As before failing at its first byte. For m>=2, its ending A has shift one,
so this no-match family also requires exactly m(n-m+1) comparisons. Omitting
the good-suffix heuristic therefore has a visible cost on these inputs.
In contrast, pattern B repeated m times needs one comparison per m-byte jump.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  struct Example {std::string name,text,pattern;};
  const std::vector<Example> examples{
    {"overlapping matches","aaaa","aa"},{"empty pattern","abc",""},
    {"oversized pattern","ab","abc"},{"one byte","banana","a"},
    {"embedded NUL",std::string("A\0B\0B",5),std::string("\0B",2)},
    {"high bytes",std::string("\xff\x80\xff",3),std::string("\xff",1)}};
  std::print("| case | matches | visited windows | comparisons |\n| :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (const auto& example:examples) {
    const auto trace=dm::algorithms::boyer_moore_horspool_trace(example.text,example.pattern);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",example.name,trace.scan.positions,trace.scan.alignments,trace.scan.comparisons);
  }
  const std::size_t n=128;const std::string text(n,'A');
  std::print("\n| m | repeated-match comparisons | late-mismatch comparisons | late-mismatch matches | absent-byte comparisons |\n"
             "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (std::size_t m:{4,8,16,32,64}) {
    const auto full=dm::algorithms::boyer_moore_horspool_trace(text,std::string(m,'A'));
    const auto late=dm::algorithms::boyer_moore_horspool_trace(text,std::string("B")+std::string(m-1,'A'));
    const auto absent=dm::algorithms::boyer_moore_horspool_trace(text,std::string(m,'B'));
    if (full.scan.comparisons!=m*(n-m+1) || late.scan.comparisons!=m*(n-m+1) || !late.scan.positions.empty()) return 1;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",m,full.scan.comparisons,late.scan.comparisons,late.scan.positions.size(),absent.scan.comparisons);
  }
}
```
