\caption(Setting m proportional to n makes the repeated-match and late-mismatch comparison counts quadratic. More or longer skips are input-dependent, rather than a guarantee from increasing pattern length.)

> Real text: separate searches over passenger names

The built-in Titanic table contains 891 passenger records. Search each Name
separately for the five literal patterns below, with no case folding or word
boundary rules. A match cannot span records, and a passenger can contain a
pattern more than once. These counts describe substrings in this table, not
categories inferred from titles or names.

`string_search_comparison` compiles tables once per pattern, then compares
complete position vectors against a naive left-to-right scan for each record.
We retain its Horspool and naive rows. The equality flag checks positions in
every record, rather than only aggregate totals. Comparison counts exclude
preprocessing, table lookups and loop conditions; they are not elapsed times.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/horspool_titanic_comparisons.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto comparison=dm::algorithms::string_search_comparison(
      dm::datasets::titanic(),"Name",{"Mr.","Mrs.","Miss.","Master.","William"})
      .filter([](const auto& row){return row.get_string("method")!="Zhu-Takaoka";});
  for (std::size_t i=0;i<comparison.nrows();++i)
    if (comparison.double_at("agrees_with_naive",i)!=1) return 1;
  std::print("{}\n",comparison.to_md());
  const auto totals=comparison.select({"method","comparisons","alignments"}) |
      dm::group_by("method") | dm::summarise_each(dm::sum);
  std::print("\n{}\n",totals.to_md());
  const auto& counts=totals.get_column("comparisons").values();
  const double top=*std::max_element(counts.begin(),counts.end());
  dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(counts,totals.get_column<std::string>("method").values(),"byte comparisons")
      .title("Five literal queries over the same 891 passenger names")
      .x_label("search method").y_label("search byte comparisons")
      .y_limits(0,top*1.4).size(900,480).save_svg("build/horspool_titanic_comparisons.svg");
}
```
